WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Layrs begins with a Privy-authenticated user and an attested private session.

00:08.000 --> 00:18.000
The application displays only aggregate public market data. Balances, orders and positions remain inside confidential accounting.

00:18.000 --> 00:29.000
A user funds the protocol or a liquidity vault, then places a private order into the TEE-protected order book.

00:29.000 --> 00:40.000
After the market closes, Layrs derives the deterministic Pyth median outcome and publishes settlement evidence on Horizen.

00:40.000 --> 00:52.000
An asynchronous RISC Zero proof binds the market, outcome and settlement commitment without delaying execution.

00:52.000 --> 01:04.000
zkVerify verifies the receipt. Layrs publishes the proof hash and settlement commitment to its non-custodial registry on Horizen.

01:04.000 --> 01:16.000
Anyone can reproduce the verification from the public privacy-evidence repository and compare the result to the on-chain statement.

01:16.000 --> 01:24.000
Private execution. Public receipt. This is Layrs on Horizen.
